WEBVTT

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.160
I feel bad for the chief priest.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.420
Makoto-chan's only four years old.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.100
She still needs constant care.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.190
Your name's Makoto?

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.400
You can see me?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.410
That makes you the 15th.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.920
That was how I first met Gintaro.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.470
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:46.890
<b>The 15th Successor and Gintaro</b>

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.070
My home is a small Inari shrine

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.570
that's been around since the Edo period.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:04.990
Our shrine is dedicated to the god 
of agriculture, Uka-no-Mitama.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.830
Wait, what?

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:15.540
Man, what happened?

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:19.290
There's my father the 
chief priest, myself,

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:23.420
and Gintaro, the herald who serves 
as a messenger of the gods.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.740
The three of us live together.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.600
Hey, Makoto.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.480
Can you keep the noise level 
down when you wake up?

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.720
Oh, Gintaro! Good morning!

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.510
Oh, is Gintaro-sama on the roof?

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:36.440
Yup.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:41.150
I'm not fortunate enough to see him, 
since I married into the family.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.740
I hope that you will continue 
to put up with Makoto.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:52.140
Gintaro is a herald, so normal 
people can't see him.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:56.710
I can see him because I am a 
true successor of this shrine.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.860
Anyway, Makoto, 
don't you need to go to school?

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.370
Right! Can you take this, Dad?!

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:03.650
Bye!

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.050
Be careful now.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:09.140
Heralds typically come in pairs,

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:14.100
but it sounds like his 
partner left a century ago,

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.820
so Gintaro is the only 
herald at our shrine.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.800
Still, what's important is 
that you have faith,

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.520
so our shrine isn't any worse off.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:31.090
Wait! I need to...

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:39.260
Here's a special charm.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.430
This will help you get better.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:42.770
Yep.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:46.150
Oh, it's Makoto-oneechan!

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:49.450
Good morning, onee-chan!

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.180
Good morning, Sa-chan and Aki-chan!

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.550
What happened to that cat?

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:56.800
She's hurt,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.250
so we're going to take care of 
her together until she's better.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.980
Her name is Mi-chan.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.810
I hope she gets better soon.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:04.490
Uh-huh!

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:05.780
Oh!

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.130
I need to be somewhere, 
so I'll talk to you later!

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.740
Bye-bye!

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.630
She must be late again.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.380
Shinto West 
Public High 
School

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:22.420
Stand.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:24.030
Bow.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.340
Saeki, see me in the faculty office.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.050
Busted!

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:34.980
Seriously?

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:39.040
And the new term just started...

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.360
Saeki.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:40.940
Oh, um...

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.570
I'm Yumi. Ikegami Yumi.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.400
We need to talk.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.110
Wh-What is it?

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:50.570
I hear that you can tell fortunes.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.660
Gin!

00:05:58.510 --> 00:05:59.750
Gin!

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:02.350
Where are you?!

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.210
Gin?

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:07.170
Gin?

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.050
Fool.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.910
Gintaro!

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:16.810
Why would I be down there?

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:20.520
I need you to look at 
a classmate for me!

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.860
Do you understand what 
it means to be a herald?

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:25.990
I'll give you an orange.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.260
Don't mess around. 
Ordinary people can't see you.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:59.230
She got in a fight with her boyfriend?

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:21.870
Well?

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:25.090
Eh, she'll probably be fine.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.050
Really?

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:30.120
Yeah, her boyfriend is also sorry.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:32.230
But I'd warn her:

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:35.500
This girl is pretty stubborn.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.730
She needs to be humble 
when approaching...

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:40.180
Really?!  Awesome!

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:41.720
Great news, Yumi!

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:44.270
See? Aren't you glad you talked to her?

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:45.480
Um, try to be humble 
when you apologize...

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.360
See ya around, Saeki.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.760
Thanks.

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:49.760
Be humble!

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.450
Try to be humble...

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:56.640
Man, you're the first priest 
to abuse a herald like this.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:00.220
Yuuko was more composed and ladylike.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:03.620
Don't compare me to Mom...

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:08.280
Anyway, I'm never doing 
anything like this again.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.590
Oranges or not.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.550
Fine.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:14.740
Give me another one.

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:16.980
I'm out.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.260
What?!

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:19.810
Really?

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.690
<i>I wonder why he likes oranges.</i>

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:35.500
Oh, Ikegami-san...

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:43.360
Fraud! You said everything 
would be fine if I apologized!

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:46.440
I apologized just like you said!

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:49.650
I even said I was sorry!

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.050
No way...

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:00.100
The girl you just looked at said 
that my advice made things worse!

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.880
You said she would be fine!

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.970
Huh? That's not my problem.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:08.190
The future isn't set in stone.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.100
How can you say that?

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:13.770
Everyone comes here asking for 
help because you're always right!

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:15.450
You're the one who's always 
asking me for help.

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:22.210
Besides, you didn't give 
her the entire message.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:26.420
Well...

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:29.320
Man, some people make me laugh.

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:32.680
They never visit shrines,

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:35.350
but when in trouble, 
they turn to the gods?

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:38.840
Give me a break.

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:41.850
What's wrong with that?!

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:43.290
That's what this shrine is for!

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.520
It's a place for people to 
come when they're in trouble!

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:49.730
It doesn't help when you can't 
tell fortunes the way Yuuko did.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.200
Well!

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:55.430
You call yourself a herald, 
but you're just a stupid fox!

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.900
Yeah, that's right.

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:04.830
I'm just a mischievous old fox.

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:08.240
I fooled you all good.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.540
Serves you right.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:12.000
Wh-What's that?

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.800
Stupid Gin!

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.250
I hate you!

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:20.400
Go away!

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:23.140
Oh, really now?

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:26.140
You need me more than I need you.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.030
I don't care!

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:28.980
Just leave!

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.060
Offering Box

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:15.040
Makoto-oneechan!

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.870
We can't find Mi-chan!

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:20.600
Mi-chan disappeared!

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:22.550
Are you talking about the 
cat that was in the park?

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:27.060
She's almost recovered 
from being hit by a car.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:30.840
Please help us! 
You can find her, right?

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:33.830
You helped me find my mom's ring!

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:36.340
But that was because...

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:40.620
Onee-chan?

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:41.670
It's okay.

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:43.450
I'll help you look for her.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.480
Can you tell me where 
Mi-chan might be?

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:46.260
Uh-huh.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:50.480
Wow, it's filthy.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:55.440
This tiny shrine should be outside 
of Inari's jurisdiction.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:00.400
There used to be Inari shrines 
all over the place...

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:06.310
This place has changed quite a bit.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:10.960
Oh, it's the cat lady!

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:13.280
Sa-chan! Aki-chan!

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:15.550
Onee-chan!

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:16.920
Did you find Mi-chan?!

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:19.380
No, I can't find her.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:23.710
Ugh, Saeki?!

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:24.760
Ikegami-san?

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.980
Are you friends?

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:31.680
She took Mi-chan to the hospital.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:34.920
What do you want me to do?

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.190
I'm not going to leave an 
injured cat lying around.

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:42.090
Anyway, let's look for Mi-chan!

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:43.260
Uh-huh!

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:45.570
Don't just stand there, Saeki!

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:53.380
What's wrong, John?

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:54.710
What are you barking at?

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:57.420
Wh-What's this?

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:07.940
Actually, there's no need 
for me to avoid those.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:09.000
Oh.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.680
<b>Shoubai Grand Shrine</b>

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.680
Right, they live in this area.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:13.430
You got in a fight with your priest?

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:16.110
She's not a priest yet.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:21.240
A herald can't let a human abuse him.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:25.450
We heralds only exist because 
of the gods we serve.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:27.620
The same can be said of shrines.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:29.310
A shrine without a herald

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:32.780
will quickly crumble as the 
gods' presence fades away.

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:36.860
You should return to your own shrine.

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:38.910
Thanks for having me.

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:45.430
Oh, what happened to your partner?

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:49.890
Heralds are meant to be paired.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.780
He's gone.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:55.840
He's been gone a long time.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.700
This is all I could find.

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:03.700
She's still hurt, so she 
couldn't have gone far.

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:05.970
This is Mi-chan's!

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:09.580
Sa-chan and I drew this 
to help her get better!

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:13.910
Makoto-oneechan, use your fortune 
telling to find Mi-chan!

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.840
Please, onee-chan!

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:21.290
That's...

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:22.900
Forget it.

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:25.590
Her fortunes are totally wrong.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.200
But she was right before!

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.590
I'll check with the animal shelters.

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:32.620
What do we do?

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:34.220
Mi-chan...

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.740
We'll find her soon.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.730
Stupid Gin!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.060
I hate you!

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:43.280
Go away!

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:49.700
Yes, that's what I said!

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:49.110
I'm sorry.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.480
I was wrong.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:54.090
It's a little overweight, and her legs are wounded...

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:52.830
Can you wait a little longer?

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:55.140
Onee-chan?!

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:55.870
Saeki?!

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:04.820
Bah, I'm supposed to be the boss here.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:08.060
It doesn't matter if Makoto's upset.

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:09.760
Gintaro!

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:13.490
Gintaro!

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.250
Gin!

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:22.610
Where are you, Gintaro?!

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:24.520
Please show yourself!

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.370
Gin!

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.980
Come on, Gin!

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:31.490
What's wrong?

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:35.830
Have you seen Gintaro, Dad?

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:36.960
What?

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:40.000
Well, I can't see him...

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:42.460
Is he gone?

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.460
What do I do, Dad?

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:51.380
I can't find Mi-chan 
without Gin's help!

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:54.850
Now calm down and start 
from the beginning.

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:54.850
Oh, she wants me to tell 
fortunes for her again?

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:58.770
Don't worry. He'll be back soon.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.270
He probably went out for a walk.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:06.230
I got in an argument with Gintaro 
yesterday and said terrible things.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:08.640
I said I hated him and 
told him to leave.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:12.270
It was my fault that the 
advice I gave was wrong.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:15.760
I told Gintaro that he was just a fox!

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:21.210
I wanted to apologize,

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:25.730
but Gintaro's gone!

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:30.830
I've made Gin do all kinds of silly 
things for selfish reasons.

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:33.660
There are people out there 
who truly need Gin's help,

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.640
but I didn't realize that!

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:43.640
Maybe I'm just crazy,

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.300
and Gin never existed.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:46.940
Now, now.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.570
If you say that,

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:52.010
Gintaro-sama really will leave.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:58.740
Makoto, have you ever thought 
about why you're the

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:00.700
only one who can see Gintaro-sama?

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:03.410
No...

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:10.710
I don't believe that it's wrong 
of you to ask Gintaro-sama

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:13.280
to help you tell fortunes.

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:18.160
I believe it's your role 
to serve as an intermediary

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:21.530
between Gintaro-sama's 
world and the human world.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:24.850
An intermediary?

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:29.620
You have the ability to 
see Gintaro the herald.

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:32.820
You have the ability 
to relay his words.

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:36.240
I want you to consider what that means.

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:39.950
Or something like that.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:46.760
Dad, I'm going to go look for Gin!

00:17:46.760 --> 00:17:48.650
I'll apologize for what 
I said yesterday!

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:50.670
And then... And then...

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:53.630
There are kids who need Gin's help!

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:56.680
I'm the only one who can find Gin!

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:59.260
Don't stay out too late!

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:01.640
Oh, Dad!

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:03.680
Can you have a bunch of oranges ready?!

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:05.600
Of course.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:08.100
Gintaro-sama loves oranges.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:12.740
<i>Gin...</i>

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:15.030
<i>I'm sorry, Gin.</i>

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:18.290
<i>I should know better after being 
with you since I was little.</i>

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:22.000
<i>No, I've been with you 
for such a long time,</i>

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:25.300
<i>that I forgot you were a 
messenger from the gods.</i>

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:30.250
<i>I have to find Gintaro 
and say I'm sorry!</i>

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.730
Gin!

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:33.730
Where are you, Gin?!

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.730
Gin?!

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:41.410
Man, where does she think I went?

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:43.310
That girl doesn't use her head.

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:49.770
Hey! Don't mess up my fields!

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:51.380
Damn fox!

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:53.770
Never come back!

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:02.150
What's the matter?

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:08.300
I can only offer you an orange.

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:11.500
But please help yourself.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:29.350
Damn, come on now!

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:37.050
Gin...

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:40.200
Gintaro?

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:45.740
Fool!

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:53.880
Man, why would I be down there?

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:56.340
Gin...

00:19:56.700 --> 00:19:58.350
Gintaro...

00:19:58.350 --> 00:19:59.720
I found you!

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:02.300
I finally found you!

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:04.790
Stupid!

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:08.720
I was worried, stupid Gintaro!

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:13.750
Wait, that's not what 
I wanted to say.

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:15.720
Um...

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:18.120
I'm sorry about what I said yesterday.

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:19.300
Oh, right.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.460
What do I do?!

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:23.300
The cat's gone! Mi-chan's missing!

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:25.090
Guess I'll have to step in.

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:28.870
You can't do anything without me.

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:33.070
I'm expecting enough 
oranges to make me full.

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:02.320
Sa-chan and Aki-chan were thrilled.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.750
What's surprising, though,

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:09.280
is the fact that Ikegami-san's 
boyfriend found Mi-chan first.

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:12.440
Her bandages came off 
before she was healed,

00:21:12.440 --> 00:21:13.710
and he couldn't ignore her.

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:16.080
It looks like Ikegami-san 
was able to make up

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.330
with her boyfriend in the end.

00:21:24.730 --> 00:21:27.140
So, um...

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:30.560
Thank you, Gin.

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:35.520
What is it?

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:41.470
I've spent centuries 
serving the god Inari,

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:45.490
but the priests have always feared 
me, revered me, and worshiped me.

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:48.150
I've learned my lesson now.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:49.520
But to be honest...

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:53.290
I like it better this way.

00:21:58.970 --> 00:21:59.540
Gimme.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:00.160
Hmm?

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:01.290
Don't play dumb.

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:02.500
I want my oranges.

00:22:02.830 --> 00:22:04.300
Oranges.

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:08.440
Say, I'm curious.

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:09.970
Why do you like oranges?

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:13.510
I'm never going to tell you.

00:22:13.510 --> 00:22:15.080
Why not?

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:16.190
Why not?!

00:22:16.190 --> 00:22:18.510
I refuse to tell you.

00:22:18.510 --> 00:22:19.540
You don't have to be so mean!

00:22:19.540 --> 00:22:20.120
Oh, really?

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:21.940
Ow! What's that for?!

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:27.380
If you happen to be in the area, 
please stop by Saeki Shrine.

00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:30.960
You might run into my 
father, the relaxed chief priest

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:37.740
or a very lazy and gruff fox spirit.

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:18.970
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:18.970
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:15.740
An Inari shrine is a shrine for 
worshiping the god of foxes.

00:24:15.740 --> 00:24:18.970
What kind of Inari shrines 
are near where you live?

00:24:19.060 --> 00:24:24.850
<b>Learning to Compromise</b>

00:24:19.690 --> 00:24:22.060
Next time: "Learning to Compromise."

00:24:22.680 --> 00:24:24.850
May fortune be with you.
